{%- comment -%}
  UNDER page visual-parity stylesheet — SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for UNDER
  layout overrides. Contains no markup: scopes a shared frame treatment to
  the three UNDER editorial media/text sections by section id. An earlier
  version of this file existed under this same name/path but was removed
  by later work on the page (gone from templates/collection.under.json's
  section order as of this task); this replaces it rather than adding a
  second competing system.

  Values were measured live against the current official reference
  (hair.montibello.com/gama/under/), not carried over from memory:
    - editorial media: 650x462px @1440px viewport (aspect-ratio 650/462),
      border-radius 12px, object-fit: cover — identical numbers to the
      HOP/Luxlight editorial media-frame fix (sections/montibello-hop-
      luxlight-media-frame.liquid), confirmed by measuring UNDER's
      official page separately. Deliberately a SEPARATE file, scoped only
      to UNDER's section ids, rather than extending that HOP/Luxlight file
      — kept as two single-purpose files instead of one multi-page file,
      per this task's instruction not to touch the HOP/Luxlight file.
    - 2-column container: max-width 1300px, column-gap ~48px (visual gap
      to the text column; official implements it as inner text padding,
      applied here as column-gap for the same rendered result)
    - orientation (media_position) already matches official section-by-
      section as configured in templates/collection.under.json — left /
      right / left for stats+carta / Glucamine / Elevated Warmth — and is
      NOT touched here, only frame size/radius.

  Glucamine (glucamine_under) already carries `media_style: framed`, a
  shared modifier on montibello-image-banner.liquid used elsewhere at a
  DIFFERENT radius/ratio (24px, 1350:1080) — that shared rule is not
  edited (other pages use it), it's overridden here at higher specificity
  for this one section id only, matching the measured 12px/650:462 like
  its two UNDER siblings.

  MANAGER FEEDBACK SPRINT (Perú vs España annotated review) added the
  heading-size, spacing and background rules below — previously
  unaddressed in this file. Same measured values as the HOP/Luxlight/
  subfamily sibling file (sections/montibello-hop-luxlight-media-frame.liquid):
  40px/35px heading size, rgb(246, 246, 243) background, 56px row spacing.
  Peru's Glucamine/Elevated Warmth headings measured 48px today, confirming
  the manager's note.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  :is(
    [id$='__stats_carta_under'],
    [id$='__glucamine_under'],
    [id$='__elevated_warmth_under']
  ) {
    background-color: rgb(246, 246, 243);
  }

  :is(
    [id$='__stats_carta_under'],
    [id$='__glucamine_under'],
    [id$='__elevated_warmth_under']
  ) :is(h1, h2, h3) {
    font-size: 35px !important;
    font-weight: 700 !important;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      font-size: 40px !important;
    }
  }

  :is(
    [id$='__stats_carta_under'],
    [id$='__glucamine_under'],
    [id$='__elevated_warmth_under']
  ) :is(
    .montibello-stats,
    .montibello-banner--split,
    .montibello-feature-rows
  ) {
    max-width: 1300px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      /* Base component defaults to `align-items: stretch`, which would
         stretch the media box to match the text column's natural
         height instead of holding the measured 650:462 ratio. */
      align-items: center;
    }
  }

  :is(
    [id$='__stats_carta_under'],
    [id$='__glucamine_under'],
    [id$='__elevated_warmth_under']
  ) :is(
    .montibello-stats__media,
    .montibello-banner__media,
    .montibello-feature-rows__media
  ) {
    /* `width: 100%` alongside `aspect-ratio`: without a definite width,
       the stretched-height box (see align-items note above, and any
       leftover min-height from the base component) would derive its
       width FROM height via the ratio instead of from the grid track,
       producing inconsistent frame sizes per section. */
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 650 / 462;
    /* `!important`: montibello-banner--framed (glucamine's `media_style`)
       sets border-radius: 24px at the same specificity as this rule and
       would otherwise win the cascade tie by later source order. */
    min-height: 0 !important;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 12px !important;
    overflow: hidden;

    @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

